CAT = "fladjPip"; SEG = "PIP"
Q = [
("Florida personal injury protection disability benefits pay what share of the injured person's lost gross income?",
 "60 percent", ["80 percent", "66 2/3 percent", "50 percent"],
 "s. 627.736(1)(b) pays 60 percent of lost gross income and earning capacity, plus replacement services. The 80 percent figure is the medical benefit."),
("Florida personal injury protection disability benefits must be paid at least once every:",
 "2 weeks", ["Week", "Month", "Calendar quarter"],
 "s. 627.736(1)(b) requires all disability benefits to be paid at least every 2 weeks."),
("A Florida PIP benefit becomes overdue if not paid within how long after the insurer gets written notice of a covered loss and its amount?",
 "30 days", ["15 days", "45 days", "60 days"],
 "Under s. 627.736(4)(b), PIP benefits are overdue if not paid within 30 days after written notice of the fact and amount of a covered loss; overdue payments bear interest."),
("A Florida PIP insurer reasonably suspects fraud and notifies the claimant within the first 30 days. How much more time does it have to investigate?",
 "60 days", ["30 days", "90 days", "10 days"],
 "s. 627.736(4)(i) gives the insurer an additional 60 days, beginning at the end of the initial 30-day period, to conduct its fraud investigation."),
("Florida PIP medical benefits do not reimburse:",
 "Massage therapy or acupuncture", ["Ambulance rides and hospital care", "Dental work and X-rays", "Rehabilitative services"],
 "s. 627.736(1)(a)5. excludes massage therapy and acupuncture from PIP medical benefits, whoever provides them."),
("Which injured person may a Florida PIP insurer exclude from benefits?",
 "One hurt while committing a felony", ["A passenger in the insured car", "A relative living with the insured", "A pedestrian hit by the insured car"],
 "s. 627.736(2)(b) allows exclusion of a person who intentionally caused his or her own injury or was injured while committing a felony."),
("Under Florida's no-fault tort exemption, a person hurt in a car accident may recover damages for pain and suffering only if the injury includes:",
 "A permanent injury or death", ["Treatment begun within 14 days", "Bills over the PIP limit", "A police crash report"],
 "s. 627.737(2) limits pain and suffering damages to significant and permanent loss of an important bodily function, permanent injury, significant and permanent scarring or disfigurement, or death."),
("Under Florida law, a rental company's liability and PIP insurance on a rented car is primary unless:",
 "The agreement says so in 10-point type", ["The renter has a personal auto policy too", "The rental lasts for under one week", "The renter is younger than age 25"],
 "s. 627.7263 makes the lessor's coverage primary unless the rental or lease agreement states otherwise in at least 10-point type on its face."),
("A car is leased for two years and the lessor provides the liability coverage. Who may reject Florida uninsured motorist coverage?",
 "Only the lessee", ["Only the lessor", "Either party alone", "Neither of them"],
 "s. 627.727(1) gives the lessee of a vehicle leased for 1 year or longer the sole privilege to reject UM coverage or select lower limits when the lessor provides the liability coverage."),
("Florida PIP medical reimbursement is capped at a lower amount when a provider determines the injured person:",
 "Had no emergency medical condition", ["Was partly at fault for causing the crash", "Has other health insurance too", "Was a passenger, not a driver"],
 "s. 627.736(1)(a)3. and 4. allow the full medical limit only if an authorized provider finds an emergency medical condition; without one the reimbursement is limited to a lower amount."),
("Florida PIP death benefits are paid:",
 "In addition to medical and disability", ["Instead of medical benefits", "Only when the insured was not at fault", "Only to a surviving spouse"],
 "s. 627.736(1)(c) states death benefits are in addition to the medical and disability benefits, and may go to the estate, relatives or another person equitably entitled."),
("When a Florida PIP insurer pays only part of a claim or rejects it, it must give the claimant:",
 "An itemized specification", ["A refund of the premium", "A new claim number only", "A copy of the crash report"],
 "s. 627.736(4)(b)2. requires an itemized specification of each item the insurer had reason to dispute or reject, with the reasons."),
]
